st1=storypage('lost','HEAVEN LOST','Ślokas 2.1–8',
 panels('Three panels: gods and asuras at war; the buffalo demon on Indra’s throne; the gods going to Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva for help',[
  ('#ffe3c4','100 YEARS OF WAR',GODS(150,.5,3,30,40)+ASURA(110,150,.8)+ASURA(130,150,.7,'#3a2a6a')+T(72,40,'⚔',30)),
  ('#fff3b0','MAHIṢA AS INDRA','<rect x="30" y="50" width="86" height="70" fill="#ffd60a" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>'+BUFFALO(72,100,.9)),
  ('#dfe9f6','“HELP US”',GOD(30,150,.6,'#ffd60a','#3b6fd0')+GOD(60,150,.6,'#fff','#9fd3f0')+BRAHMA(110,120,.6)+GODS(170,.35,4,20,30))]),
 ['<b>The war.</b> Gods and asuras fight for a full hundred years. Mahiṣa leads the asuras; Indra leads the gods.',
  '<b>The defeat.</b> The gods lose. Mahiṣāsura becomes Indra and sits on the throne of heaven.',
  '<b>To the great gods.</b> Led by Brahmā, the defeated gods go to Śiva and Viṣṇu (“the one with Garuḍa on his banner”).',
  '<b>The complaint.</b> “He has taken over the offices of the Sun, Indra, Fire, Wind, Moon, Yama and Varuṇa. We wander the earth like mortals.”',
  '<b>The plea.</b> “We have come to you for refuge. Think how he can be killed.”'],
 ("Why couldn't the great gods just fight him?","Mahiṣa had a boon: in the usual telling, no man or god could kill him. Watch what the gods do instead. They give up their power to someone new."),
 'Heaven is lost; <b>the gods seek refuge</b>.')
st2=storypage('gifts','EVERY GOD GIVES','Ślokas 2.19–31 · the full list',
 panels('Three panels: the gods lining up with weapons; jewels and garments from the milky ocean; the Goddess, fully armed, on her lion',[
  ('#fde4e4','WEAPONS',TRIDENT(30,90,.8)+'<circle cx="72" cy="60" r="14" fill="#ffd60a" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>'+SWORD(110,140,20,1)+'<path d="M60 150 q12 -16 26 0 q-12 8 -26 0z" fill="#fff" stroke="#111"/>'),
  ('#e3f2fd','JEWELS','<circle cx="72" cy="80" r="40" fill="none" stroke="#e0a800" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>'+''.join(f'<circle cx="{40+k*16}" cy="{140}" r="6" fill="{c}" stroke="#111"/>' for k,c in enumerate(['#c0392b','#2a9d6f','#3b6fd0','#ffd60a','#fff']))),
  ('#fff3b0','READY',DEVI(72,0,.75)+LION(72,160,.6))]),
 ['<b>Weapons.</b> Śiva a trident, Viṣṇu a discus, Varuṇa a conch and noose, Agni a spear, Vāyu a bow and quivers, Indra a thunderbolt and bell, Yama a staff.',
  '<b>Prayer tools.</b> Brahmā a rosary and water pot. The Sun puts his rays into her skin. Kāla (Time) gives a sword and a spotless shield.',
  '<b>Jewels.</b> The milky ocean gives a necklace, unageing garments, a crest-jewel, earrings, bangles, a crescent moon ornament, armlets, anklets and rings.',
  '<b>More.</b> Viśvakarmā, the divine craftsman, an axe, many missiles and unbreakable armour; the ocean lotus garlands; Śeṣa a serpent necklace set with jewels.',
  '<b>Mount and cup.</b> Himavān gives the lion and jewels; Kubera a cup never empty. Honoured by all, she laughs aloud.'],
 ("Why does every god give something?","Because victory needs everyone. Each gives his best, and none is diminished: Śiva and Viṣṇu draw new weapons out of their own. She carries the whole of heaven's strength."),
 'All of heaven’s strength, <b>in her hands</b>.')
st3=storypage('battle','THE ARMIES FALL','Ślokas 2.40–69',
 panels('Three panels: vast asura armies with chariots and elephants charging; the Goddess and her lion scattering them; flowers falling from the sky',[
  ('#ffe3c4','CROWDS OF CROWDS',CHARIOT(40,150,.7)+CHARIOT(100,150,.7)+ASURA(72,110,.7)+ASURA(30,100,.6,'#3a2a6a')+ASURA(118,100,.6)),
  ('#fde4e4','LIKE FIRE IN A FOREST',DEVI(72,0,.6)+LION(72,150,.6)+'<path d="M10 180 q20 -40 30 0 q10 -40 30 0 q10 -40 30 0 q10 -40 30 0" fill="#ff8c1a" stroke="#111"/>'),
  ('#e3f2fd','FLOWERS FROM HEAVEN',''.join(f'<text x="{(29*k)%130+6}" y="{(31*k)%150+20}" font-size="14">🌸</text>' for k in range(14)))]),
 ['<b>The generals.</b> Cikṣura leads the asura army; Cāmara, Udagra, Mahāhanu, Asiloma, Bāṣkala, Biḍāla and others come with chariots, elephants and horses beyond counting.',
  '<b>Mahiṣa himself</b> stands in the middle, surrounded by “thousands of crores of crores” of chariots, elephants and horses.',
  '<b>The Goddess answers.</b> She cuts their weapons as if at play; her breaths become armies; her lion roams the enemy “like fire in a forest”.',
  '<b>A festival of war.</b> Her gaṇas beat drums and blow conches. The bell stuns, the noose binds, the trident and mace cut down the asuras.',
  '<b>The end of the army.</b> In a moment she destroys it all, as fire burns a great heap of grass and wood. The gods shower flowers from heaven.'],
 ("All those generals, and she beat them in a moment?","Their numbers are huge on purpose: crores upon crores. The point is not arithmetic. However large the forces of ego, they are like dry grass before her fire."),
 'However vast the army, <b>dry grass before her fire</b>.')
P=dict(n=7,ch=2,out='/home/claude/work/devim/Devi_Mahatmya_Part07.html',
 title='The Goddess Is Born · Part 7 · Devī Māhātmya series · srini.presents',
 desc='Devī Māhātmya, Part 7: chapter 2. Mahiṣāsura takes heaven, the anger of the gods becomes a mountain of light, the Goddess is born from it, receives every god’s weapon and destroys the asura armies. Explained in plain English with illustrations.',
 h1='THE GODDESS IS BORN',series='DEVĪ MĀHĀTMYA · PART 7 · CHAPTER 2',tag='From the light of all the gods · explained and illustrated',cover=cover,
 how='The story in <b>comic panels</b>, and the key ślokas of chapter 2 on their own pages: the chant, a picture, what it says, the key words, one insight and the one thing to remember.',
 where=[f'In {plink(6)}, the first carita ended: Mahāmāyā held Viṣṇu in sleep, then woke him, and Madhu and Kaiṭabha fell.',
  'Now the <b>second carita</b> begins, whose deity is <b>Mahālakṣmī</b>. A buffalo demon, Mahiṣa, has conquered heaven. The gods’ anger becomes light, the light becomes a woman, and every god arms her. This is the birth scene of the Goddess, loved across India.'],
 wtalk=("A goddess made of light?","Made of all the gods' light. Each one gives his power, and together they become her. Read chapter 2 as a picture of what unity can do."),
 fulls=[('THE KEY VERSES IN ONE GO','Chapter 2, ślokas 2–21',V[:7]),('IN ONE GO · CONTINUED','Chapter 2, ślokas 22–53',V[7:])],
 fullnote='Text as given in the Devīmāhātmyam edition of devimahatmyam.aurobharati.in (69 ślokas in chapter 2); its numbering is followed. Editions number them slightly differently.',
 seq=[st1]+V[:6]+[st2]+V[6:12]+V[12:]+[st3],
 toc=[('THE STORY',[('lost','Heaven Lost')]),('THE BIRTH',V[:6]),('THE GIFTS',[('gifts','Every God Gives')]+V[6:12]),('THE BATTLE',V[12:]+[('battle','The Armies Fall')])],
 end=['<b>Heaven lost (2.1–8).</b> After a hundred years of war Mahiṣa becomes Indra; the gods go to Viṣṇu and Śiva for refuge.',
  '<b>The light (2.9–13).</b> The gods’ anger becomes radiance, the radiance a blazing mountain, and the mountain a woman filling the three worlds.',
  '<b>The body (2.14–18).</b> Each god gives a part of her: Śiva her face, Viṣṇu her arms, Agni her three eyes.',
  '<b>The gifts (2.19–35).</b> Every god gives a weapon or jewel; Himavān the lion. She laughs, and the worlds shake. “Jaya!”',
  '<b>The battle (2.36–69).</b> Mahiṣa sees her cosmic form; his generals and armies fall like grass before fire.'],
 endsub='Chapter 2 in five lines',
 next=("What's next?",'Part 8: chapter 3. Mahiṣa himself fights, changing shape again and again: buffalo, lion, man, elephant. The Goddess drinks, laughs, and says: “Roar, fool, roar, while I drink.”'),
 endkey='<b>the strength of all, united, becomes the Goddess</b>.',
 foot='Study notes on the Devī Māhātmya, chapter 2 (Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa). The story is retold in our words; ślokas are given as in the Devīmāhātmyam edition of devimahatmyam.aurobharati.in, whose numbering is followed. Mahiṣa’s boon is from the wider Purāṇic tradition, not from chapter 2 itself. Meanings are our own plain-English renderings. Zappy and Prof. Bolt are fictional.')
